%S A400921 1,1,2,5,14,41,127,410,1353,4576,15732,54874,193639,690206,2480944,
%T A400921 8983629,32738382,119980438,441907696,1634900899,6072852892,
%U A400921 22639586343,84678626063,317675277518,1195054404545,4507028566536,17037513370281,64544586785104
%N A400921 Number of monosubstituted acyclic hydrocarbons (alkanes and olefins), ignoring stereoisomers.
%C A400921 Equivalent to the number of rooted multigraph trees, in which the root node has out-degree <= 3 and internal nodes have degree <= 4, each edge has multiplicity <= 2, and no node is adjacent to two edges both with multiplicity 2. In the chemical interpretation, the final restriction excludes allenes and cumulenes, which have low stability compared to the classes considered here.
%C A400921 Ignoring stereoisomers means that the children of a node are unordered. They can be permuted in any way and it is still the same tree. See A400922 for the analogous sequence with stereoisomers counted.
%C A400921 A000598 is the analogous sequence considering only alkanes.
%H A400921 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A400921/b400921.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A400921 Casper Asbjørn Eriksen and Daniel Merkle, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02932">Enumerating Chemical Structures, Stereoisomers, and Stereogenic Units with Analytic Combinatorics</a>, arXiv:2609.02932 [physics.chem-ph], 2026.
%H A400921 Casper Asbjørn Eriksen, <a href="https://gitlab.com/casbjorn/molenum">Python Notebook</a> (0.2.0).
%F A400921 G.f.: A(x) satisfies A(x) = 1 + x*((1 + 3*x)*A(x)^3 + 3*(1 + x)*A(x)*A(x^2) + 2*A(x^3))/6. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 22 2026
%o A400921 (PARI) seq(n) = {my(g=O(1)); for(n=0, n, g = 1 + x*((1+3*x)*g^3 + 3*(1 + x)*g*subst(g,x,x^2) + 2*subst(g,x,x^3))/6 ); Vec(g)} \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 22 2026
%Y A400921 Cf. A000598, A400922, A400923.
%K A400921 nonn,new
%O A400921 0,3
